<title>FINLAND: Rauma's Neles wins its largest order.</title>
<headline>Rauma's Neles wins its largest order.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Rauma Oy said in a statement on Monday its Neles-Jamesbury had won its largest-ever single order -- supply control and manual shut-off valves for APRIL group's pulp and paper operations in Indonesia.</p>
<p>It did not give the value of the deal but a Rauma official said its previously largest orders had been worth &quot;roughly 50 to 60 million markka&quot;.</p>
</text>
